In [Mn($H_{2}$O)_{6}]^{2+}

$Mn^{+2}$ = [Ar] $3d^{5} 4s^{0}$ <img src="https://neetcare-image.cdn.examgoal.net/1qpqahkk8sywc68/6f60b794-00f2-4f16-88c1-da15bca5124f/fb381a00-7a7d-11ea-aedc-f1c8d8e0194b/file-1qpqahkk8sywc69-424w.png" style="max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;" loading="lazy" alt="AIPMT 2004 Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 38 English Explanation">

In presence of weak field ligand $H_{2}$O, there will be no pairing of electrons. So it will form a high spin complex, i.e. the number of unpaired electrons = 5.
